# /sdd-next

Purpose:
  Advance to the next decision step or case from completion-checked state.

Owns: commands\sdd-next.sdd
Description:
  Advance to the next decision step or case.
  Checks completion status of current decision and linked tasks
  before determining the next action.

Usage:
  /sdd-next
  /sdd-next --step
  /sdd-next --subtask
  /sdd-next --decision DEC-<ID>
  /sdd-next --case CASE-<ID>
  /sdd-next --force
  /sdd-next --approve [--id DP-<ID>]
  /sdd-next --review [--id DP-<ID>]
  /sdd-next --status

Options:
  --step      Delivery-chain step mode (DL1): continue the immutable
              workflow from the saved state — execute ONE step only
  --subtask   Unit mode: resolve the NEXT executable SUBTASK from
              the current DEC -> TASK -> SUBTASK state and execute
              ONLY that unit through its lifecycle (see SubtaskMode)
  --decision  Advance specific decision
  --case      Jump to specific case
  --force     Force advance even if incomplete (requires approval)
  --approve   Auto-approve and proceed from Decision Point (CONTINUE/REVIEW types; pauses at GATE/DECISION/ERROR).
              Optionally targets a specific Decision Point: --approve --id DP-<ID>
  --review    Enter review mode at current Decision Point for modification.
              Optionally targets a specific Decision Point: --review --id DP-<ID>
  --status    List all Decision Points and their current state

InitialLoad (Phase 151 — EXPAND protocol):
  - .sdd/INDEX.sdd (routing only)
  - saved workflow state (.specdd/delivery/{run_id}/state.sdd; or
    tasks/INDEX.sdd for decision mode)
  - .sdd/workflow/step-keys.sdd (dictionary — step mode only)
  - .specdd/state/current.sdd (STATE pointer — subtask mode reads
    it FIRST, [SF1]; missing/stale => scan fallback)
  Step specs, stage details, and gates load on EXPAND only.

StepMode (Phase 151 — the stateful /next):
  Applies to delivery chain DL1 (@../chains/delivery.sdd) with canonical
  step keys (@../workflow/step-keys.sdd). On every /next:
    1. READ the saved workflow state (chains/delivery.sdd StepState;
       .specdd/delivery/{run_id}/state.sdd)
    2. RE-ANALYZE the relevant project files (state is truth, not chat)
    3. IDENTIFY the last completed step
    4. IDENTIFY the first incomplete step
    5. EXECUTE ONLY that step
    6. VERIFY its result (DONE criteria: input exists, work completed,
       output artifact exists, internally consistent, validation passed)
    7. UPDATE the workflow state
    8. STOP
  Rules:
    - Called 100 times -> continues from the actual last state EVERY time.
    - NEVER restarts from BC unless the workflow state explicitly requires it.
    - If a blocking BUG exists (BUG-REGISTRY.sdd), /next returns the
      blocked step — it MUST NOT advance past it.
    - Never ask the user what is next — determine from saved state + project.
  Step-mode output:
    [step_mode: delivery]
    [current_step: <key>]  [last_completed: <key>]  [first_incomplete: <key>]
    [blocking_bugs: <ids|none>]
    [action: execute_one_step]
    [result: <step outcome + DONE-evidence>]

SubtaskMode (Phase 155 — the unit-level /next):
  Resolves the next executable SUBTASK (smallest execution unit,
  bax ../tasks/SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd, ../schemas/subtask.sdd).
  Algorithm:
    1. READ STATE first (.specdd/state/current.sdd, [SF1]); if
       missing or stale, scan decisions/ and tasks/ to rebuild it
       ([SF3] — project files win)
    2. FIND the first task (dependency order — readiness semantics
       of dependencies/graph.sdd) that has a TODO subtask; if the
       STATE's current subtask is mid-lifecycle (not DONE), resume
       THAT unit — never jump units
    3. A BLOCKED subtask is reported with its blocker — /next does
       NOT advance past it (mirrors step-mode BUG blocking)
    4. RESOLVE and output the unit with its parent context
    5. EXECUTE only that unit through its lifecycle gates (CR ->
       RF -> SC -> TS, v2 ordering); unit DONE requires done-proof
    6. UPDATE STATE ([SF2]); the next /sdd-next --subtask call
       resolves the next unit
  Task completion rule: a task is complete ONLY when ALL its
  subtasks are DONE (extends existing task_complete check).
  Subtask-mode output:
    [subtask_mode: unit]
    [decision: DEC-XXX]  [task: TASK-XXX]  [subtask: SUBTASK-XXX]
    [state: <lifecycle state>]  [blocked: <reason|none>]
    [context: parent DEC + TASK references]
    [action: execute_one_unit]
    [result: <unit outcome + done-proof evidence on DONE>]

Behavior:
  1. Read current decision state from projects/{project_name}/decisions/
  2. Read linked tasks from projects/{project_name}/tasks/
  3. Check if current decision and ALL linked tasks are complete
  4. IF complete:
       - Move to next decision in the chain
       - If no more decisions, move to next case
       - If no more cases, signal workflow complete
  5. IF incomplete:
       - Identify which section is incomplete (decision or task)
       - Resume from that section
       - Do NOT advance to next case
  6. Record transition in decision history
  7. Update project state

CompletionCheck:
  decision_complete:
    - status = approved
    - all acceptance criteria met
    - implementation tasks linked

  task_complete:
    - status = DONE
    - all acceptance criteria met
    - tests pass
    - review passed

Output:
  Decision/case mode (default):
    [decision: DEC-XXX]
    [tasks_complete: true|false]
    [incomplete_section: decision|task|none]
    [action: advance|resume|complete]
    [next: <decision|case|workflow_complete>]

  Step mode (--step):
    [step_mode: delivery]
    [current_step: <key>]  [last_completed: <key>]  [first_incomplete: <key>]
    [blocking_bugs: <ids|none>]
    [action: execute_one_step]
    [result: <step outcome + DONE-evidence>]

  Subtask mode (--subtask):
    [subtask_mode: unit]
    [decision: DEC-XXX]  [task: TASK-XXX]  [subtask: SUBTASK-XXX]
    [state: <lifecycle state>]  [blocked: <reason|none>]
    [context: parent DEC + TASK references]
    [action: execute_one_unit]
    [result: <unit outcome + done-proof evidence on DONE>]

Rules:
  [NEXT-01] /sdd-next advances from saved state, never from memory.
  [NEXT-02] --approve auto-advances CONTINUE and REVIEW types; pauses at GATE, DECISION, ERROR.
  [NEXT-03] --review re-opens current stage; all context preserved.
  [NEXT-04] --status lists all Decision Points: id, type, stage, result, timestamp.
  [NEXT-05] Every Decision Point emitted by execution-runner.ts is visible via --status.
  [NEXT-06] --approve --id DP-<ID> targets a specific Decision Point for approval.
  [NEXT-07] --review --id DP-<ID> targets a specific Decision Point for review.
  [NEXT-08] GATE type requires human confirmation even with --approve.
  [NEXT-09] --approve at a GATE emits OBS18 with auto_approve:true.

Navigation:
  INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
  DeliveryChain: @../chains/delivery.sdd
  StepKeys: @../workflow/step-keys.sdd
  TaskStateMachine: @../tasks/TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
  SubtaskStateMachine: @../tasks/SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
  SubtaskSchema: @../schemas/subtask.sdd
  StateTemplate: @../templates/specdd/state.template.sdd
  BugRegistry: @../tasks/BUG-REGISTRY.sdd
  RuntimeState: @../runtime/state.sdd

State: +
   (extended with step mode / immutable DL1 continuation per Phase 151)
   (Phase 155: added --subtask unit mode with STATE read-first
    pointer; subtask blocking mirrors BUG blocking; task completion
    now requires ALL subtasks DONE)
